{
 "path": "/home/USER/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/stage1/HA-openclaw-luna6-high-ws0/frozen/held-out-2/play/users/u070/system/state/openclaw/agents/main/agent/workshop-skills/continual-arc/SKILL.md",
 "edits": [
  {
   "oldText": "description: \"Solve Continual-ARC grid instances; infer transformations from demonstrations and choose the lowest-cost exact action.\"",
   "newText": "description: \"Solve Continual-ARC grids, including noisy motif-copy, tile-classification, diagonal-stripe, and edge-continuation tasks; infer transformations from demos and choose the lowest-cost exact action.\""
  },
  {
   "oldText": "2. For noisy grids containing a distinctive single-color motif amid zeros and another background color, record the motif's colored-cell offsets from its bounding box. Search for translated copies whose motif positions all contain zeros, recoloring those matching positions with the motif color. Preserve every other cell, including the original motif and zeros/background at non-motif positions inside the bounding box. Do not assume flood-fill or neighbor propagation: test motif translations when the grid visually consists of noisy background plus one seed object.",
   "newText": "2. For a distinctive single-color motif amid zeros and another background color, when demos suggest translated copies, follow [noisy-background motif copies](noisy-motif.md)."
  },
  {
   "oldText": "4. When full-width and full-height separator lines partition a grid into equal tiles and the output dimensions match the tile layout, map each tile to one output cell. Use demonstrations to identify which in-tile feature or count determines the output; do not assume every unusual cell or single marker is positive. For the task pattern with color-8 separators, 2×3 tiles containing mostly color 3 and occasional color 2, emit 1 for a tile with at least two 2s and 3 otherwise.",
   "newText": "4. When full-width and full-height lines partition the grid into equal tiles and the output matches that layout, follow [tile classification](../tile-classification.md)."
  },
  {
   "oldText": "6. When demonstrations show color 1 marking an absent continuation at a grid edge, compare repeated rows, bands, or motif copies to infer the expected continuation and affected cells. It may be a solid suffix or only selected motif-phase positions. Color only the confirmed missing continuation cells; preserve the existing motif and unrelated cells. Check the candidate against every demo's changed and unchanged cells, and select repeated copies from that evidence—not from rightmost zeros or suffix length alone.",
   "newText": "6. When demos show color 1 marking an absent continuation at a grid edge, follow [edge continuation](edge-continuation.md)."
  }
 ]
}

